          %h2#consequences Consequences
          %p Here we collect some consequences of the countable axiom of choice.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
                coincide (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
                also separately implies this).
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rosolini+dominance"} Rosolini dominance
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
                (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
                also separately implies this).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+unions+of+countable+sets+are+countable"} countable unions of countable sets are countable
          %h2#variations Variations
          %h3#__
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi COSHEP
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} COSHEP
            \&amp;
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DC
          %p
            Unlike the full axiom of choice, countable choice is often considered to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructively
            acceptable principle. In particular, it does not imply the principle of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi COSHEP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} COSHEP
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+choice"} dependent choice
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DC
            ). In general,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DC
            is enough to justify results in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            involving
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
          %h3{:id => ""}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                    %mn 00
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{00}
          %p
            Sometimes in foundations it is useful to consider a weaker version of countable choice, called
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mn 00
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{00}
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},\mathbb{N}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            to itself contains a functional entire relation, i.e. there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(n, x_n)
            holds. In terms of surjections, the axiom states that any surjection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon X \to \mathbb{N}
            has a section if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of a product projection.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AC
                    %mn 00
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AC_{00}
            is enough to prove that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"} Dedekind real number
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+number"} Cauchy real number
            (the converse is always true).
          %h3#WCC Weak countable choice
          %p
            The axiom of
            %strong weak countable choice
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WCC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WCC
            ) states that a surjection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon X \to \mathbf{N}
            has a section if, whenever
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \neq n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimages"} preimages
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*(m)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*(n)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WCC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WCC
            follows (for different reasons) from either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WCC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WCC
            is enough to prove that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+algebra"} fundamental theorem of algebra
            in the sense that every non-constant complex polynomial has a root; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BRS"} Bridges et al (1998)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WCC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WCC
            implies that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+reals"} Dedekind reals
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+reals"} Cauchy reals
            coincide, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#King2024"} King et al (2024)
          %h3#ACN2 Another weak countable choice
          %p
            An axiom variously called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AC
                    %mi weak
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AC_{weak}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathrm{N},2}
            is countable choice for relations from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/booleans"} booleans
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            contains a functional entire relation, i.e. there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(n, x_n)
            holds. Like
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WCC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WCC
            above, this also follows from either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC
            or excluded middle. It is enough to prove the equivalence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+reals"} Dedekind reals
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+reals"} Cauchy reals
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Saving2021"} Saving et al (2021)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#King2024"} King et al (2024)
          %h3#very_weak_countable_choice Very weak countable choice
          %p
            An even weaker form of countable choice was proposed by
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#EscardoCN"} Martin Escardo
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \sqcup (\mathbf{N}\times B) \to \mathbf{N}
            has a section, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to \mathbf{N}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+subset"} decidable subset
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is an arbitrary set with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N}\times B \to \mathbf{N}
            the projection. This follows from WCC and also from the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limited+principle+of+omniscience"} limited principle of omniscience
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EscardoCN"} constructivenews discussion
          %h3#using_a_dominance Using a dominance
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \subseteq \Omega
            and restricting countable choice to the
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:\mathbb{N} \times A \to \Sigma
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            contains a functional entire relation, i.e. there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(n, x_n) = \top
          %p
            Similarly, we can express weaker versions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},\mathbb{N}}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2}
            using a dominance
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},\mathbb{N},\Sigma}
                states that any entire open relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo →
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:\mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N} \to \Sigma
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                to itself contains a functional entire relation, i.e. there exists a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(n, x_n) = \top
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
                states that any entire open relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo →
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:\mathbb{N} \times \{0, 1\} \to \Sigma
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0, 1\}
                contains a functional entire relation, i.e. there exists a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0, 1\}
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(n, x_n) = \top
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              an
              = succeed "-overt" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_C
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
              constructed out of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cuts"} Dedekind cuts
              valued in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              are equivalent.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It suffices to prove the theorem using
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},\mathbb{N},\Sigma}
              and the more general
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
            %p
              Adopting the proof of Corollary 11.4.3 from the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
              holds. The set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = \{ (q, r) \in \mathbb{Q} \times \mathbb{Q} \vert q \lt r \}
            %p
              is equivalent to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
              to the statement that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is located:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall q,r \in S.(q \lt x) \vee (x \lt r)
            %p
              Note that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (q \lt x) \vee (x \lt r)
              is expressible as an existential statement
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists b \in \{0, 1\}.(b = 0) \Rightarrow (q \lt x) \times (b = 1) \Rightarrow (x \lt r)
            %p
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b = 0) \Rightarrow (q \lt x) \times (b = 1) \Rightarrow (x \lt r)
              is
              = succeed "-open," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
              is
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
              and equality on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0, 1\}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+relation"} decidable relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              (which implies that both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg P
              are
              = succeed "-open)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              = succeed "-open" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \Rightarrow Q
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logically+equivalent"} logically equivalent
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P \wedge Q) \vee \neg P
              and thus
              = succeed "-open." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %p
              The (curried form) of the choice function from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} AC
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{AC}_{\mathbb{N},2,\Sigma}
              is then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locator"} locator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q, r \in \mathbb{Q}} (q \lt r) \to (q \lt x) + (x \lt r)
            %p
              and lemma 11.4.1 from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
              coincide.
          %h3#topos_violating_the_cac Topos violating the CAC
          %p
            One easy example is the category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh([0,1])
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object#classical_dedekind_real_numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object#cauchy_real_numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            are not isomorphic, and this is a consequence of the internal countable choice.
          %p
            Discussion
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/79807/example-of-a-topos-that-violates-countable-choice"} here
          %h3#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            To formulate a version of the axiom of countable choice in a higher category, one has to make an appropriate choice of the meaning of “epimorphism”. In most cases, it is best to choose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphisms"} effective epimorphism in an (infinity,1)-category
            or a related notion such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eso+morphisms"} eso morphisms
          %p
            There are multiple version of the axiom of countable choice, depending on what
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated+object"} truncation
            requirements, if any, are applied to the domain.
          %ul
            %li
              An
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  axiom of countable
                  = succeed "-choice" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi CC
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC_n
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %span.newWikiWord
                truncated morphism
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/truncated+morphism"} ?
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
              has a section. We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CC
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC_\infty
              for the
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong axiom of countable infinity-choice
              %em every
              morphism with codomain the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
              has a section.
          %p
            These are stronger axioms as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            increases.
          %p There are also “internal” versions of these axioms.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                (the internal logic of an
                = succeed "-topos)," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi CC
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC_n
                is “every surjection onto the natural numbers type with
                = succeed "-type" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo →
                          %mi n
                          %mi Type
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(Y:\mathbb{N}\to n Type)} \Big( \prod_{(x:\mathbb{N})} \Vert Y(x)\Vert \to \Big\Vert \prod_{(x:\mathbb{N})} Y(x) \Big\Vert \Big)
            %li
              %p
                More generally, we can replace the
                = succeed "-truncation" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
                = succeed "-truncation" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi CC
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC_{k,n}
            %li
              %p
                We can also replace the
                = succeed "-truncation" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
                = succeed "-connectedness," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    axiom of countable
                    = succeed "-connected" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resizing+axiom"} resizing axiom
          %h2#references References
          %ul
